+
+## 6. Search
+
+PostgreSQL 17 full-text search — no extra service.
+
+```sql
+-- on kb_article_versions (only published snapshots are searchable)
+search_vector tsvector GENERATED ALWAYS AS (
+      setweight(to_tsvector('english', coalesce(title,'')),   'A')
+   || setweight(to_tsvector('english', coalesce(summary,'')), 'B')
+   || setweight(to_tsvector('english', coalesce(body,'')),    'C')
+   || setweight(to_tsvector('simple',  coalesce(title,'')),   'A')   -- exact words in any language
+   || setweight(to_tsvector('simple',  coalesce(body,'')),    'D')
+) STORED;
+CREATE INDEX ix_kb_versions_search ON kb_article_versions USING gin (search_vector);
+```
+
+- The `english` part stems ("printers" finds "printer"); the `simple` part matches exact words in any
+  language (Malay content, product codes like `HP-M404`). See open question 1.
+- **Search page:** `websearch_to_tsquery` (users can type `"exact phrase"` and `-word`), ranked with
+  `ts_rank_cd`, snippet via `ts_headline` on the body.
+- **Type-ahead / suggestions:** the typed words are sanitised to `[\p{L}\p{N}]+`, stop-words dropped,
+  each turned into a prefix term and OR-ed — `printer:* | offline:* | updat:*` — so half-typed words
+  match and an article sharing any meaningful word appears, best match first. Minimum 2 words or 8
+  characters before asking.
+- Visibility (§4) is applied **in the same SQL** (join to `kb_articles` on `published_version_id`,
+  `status = 'PUBLISHED'`, visibility and company conditions), never filtered afterwards in Java —
+  otherwise "top 5" could come back with 2.
+
